    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0467" n="439" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v03/pg439"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">315/2–2053: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative at the United
                        Nations</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Lodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Department of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1953-02-20T19:04:00-05:00">February 20,
                            1953—7:04 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>541. For Hickerson, UNA. Please find out whether
                        Boheman (Sweden) would be available for position of
                    United Nations Secretary General.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d200-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lodge</hi>
                        </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d200-f1" n="1" xml:id="d200-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 940, Feb. 21, 1953, 1:52 p.m., to Stockholm, the Department cabled,
                        Hickerson to Ambassador
                        Butterworth: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Please ascertain discreetly from FonOff, and of course without commitment on our part,
                            whether Boheman would be available for post UN Secretary General.”
                        (315/2–2053)</p></quote>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
